# WS3-10. Sources: spec/02-types.md §2 ("usize/isize: pointer-sized integer"), §7 and
# spec/04 §14 (raw-to-integer value cast `usize(p)` "reads the address as a number";
# integer-to-raw cast `raw T(addr)`), spec/15 §2 (host pointer size: the host's). A
# pointer converted to usize and back must still address x on every profile.
profiles: host hosted-amiga hosted-amiga-13
expect: output
contrast: *q = 5; ==> *q = 6;
contrast-expect: output
--- output
5
--- contrast-output
6
